On Jan 17, 2008, at 12:06 AM, Timo Paulssen wrote:

> Yoav Nir schrieb:
>> coi rodo
>> jbovlaste has a distinction between "preferred only" valsi and  
>> "all" valsi.  There are, for example, 339 preferred works starting  
>> with 'c' but 598 words in general that start with 'c'.
>> I have two questions:
>> 1. What is the difference.
>
> I think, that it's not "preferred words", but rather "preferred  
> definitions", as you can have multiple definitions in - for example  
> - english for a valsi, but using votes by the jbovlaste users, the  
> most fitting definition/translation is selected.
>
>> 2. The XML export seems to export only the preferred words. How can  
>> I get an export of all words?
>
> If my assumption is right, then that wouldn't make much sense. At  
> least if you want to use the XML exported data for a dictionary or  
> lookup program.
> I can only guess, but probably the code for XML export is based on  
> the code for the dictionary export, in which case it's the only  
> sensible thing to do to filter out non-preferred words.
>  - Timo

I thought so, but the "all" words don't contain duplicates. For  
example, the word {ckupau} is in "all" words, with a good definition,  
but it doesn't appear at all in the preferred words.

I think generating a dictionary without all these words makes it  
limited.




